  "content": {
    "id": "p27-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "The volume of air in a leaking balloon is decaying exponentially. Initially there are 6 litres of air in the balloon. After 3 days, there are 4 litres of air in the balloon. How many litres of air does the balloon contain after 5 days? Answer correct to one decimal place.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$3.1$ litres",
      "worked": "Let $V(t)$ be the volume in litres after $t$ days. With $V(0)=6$, write $V(t)=6b^{kt}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}6b^{3k}&=4\\\\b^{3k}&=\\frac23\\\\3k&=\\log_b\\!\\left(\\frac23\\right)\\\\k&=\\frac13\\log_b\\!\\left(\\frac23\\right)\\end{align*}$$\n\nUsing $b^{\\log_b x}=x$,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}V(t)&=6b^{\\frac{t}{3}\\log_b(2/3)}\\\\V(t)&=6\\left(b^{\\log_b(2/3)}\\right)^{t/3}\\\\V(t)&=6\\left(\\frac23\\right)^{t/3}\\\\V(5)&=6\\left(\\frac23\\right)^{5/3}\\\\V(5)&\\approx3.1\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe balloon contains approximately $3.1$ litres after 5 days.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 80
  },
